TourStart1Title = Progress
TourStart1 = How many required steps are done. Optional steps are needed only in some cases (for example organic farms).
TourStart2Title = The steps
TourStart2 = Each line is a step, in the suggested order, with the number of cards already entered. "Do it now" opens the right page, the question mark opens it with the guide.
TourStart3Title = Next step
TourStart3 = This is the first step still to do. At the end of each guide you can go on with the next page.
TourDossier1 = The third party of the farm. If missing, create it first in Third parties with type "Farm" and the CUAA.
TourDossier2 = Date of signature of the dossier at the CAA: required.
TourDossier3 = The CAA that keeps the dossier, if any.
TourDossier4 = For organic farms: the control body.
TourDossier5 = Warehouse of the technical inputs: validated treatments take plant protection products and fertilisers out of it.
TourDossier6 = Warehouse of the harvested products: validated harvests put their lots in it.
TourPlot1 = The dossier of the farm the plot belongs to.
TourPlot2 = Municipality, section, sheet and cadastral parcel: needed by the AGEA field notebook.
TourPlot3 = The id of the graphic parcel (LPIS/IACS), if known.
TourPlot4 = Utilised agricultural area in hectares: base of the doses per hectare and of the nitrogen and copper limits.
TourPlot5 = Current organic status. The full history (notification, conversion) goes in the Organic tab of the plot.
TourPlot6 = In a nitrate vulnerable zone the register checks the nitrogen from livestock manure.
TourMachine1 = Kind of machine: tractor, sprayer, spreader...
TourMachine2 = Date of the next inspection: shown in the expiry widget.
TourMachine3 = For sprayers: number of the functional check certificate, required by the AGEA notebook.
TourMachine4 = End of the functional check: the register warns when it is expired at the date of the treatment.
TourOperator1 = If the operator uses Dolibarr, link the user.
TourOperator2 = Number of the licence for plant protection products.
TourOperator3 = Date of the licence; its end goes in the expiry widget.
TourAgrodrug1 = Registration number of the Ministry of Health: with the synced catalogue the rest of the card updates by itself.
TourAgrodrug2 = The Dolibarr product used for the stock; better with unit kg or l.
TourAgrodrug3 = Pre-harvest interval of the label; by crop it can go in the authorised uses.
TourAgrodrug4 = FRAC/IRAC/HRAC groups of the mode of action, for the resistance warnings.
TourAgrodrug5 = For organic farms: the check of the active substances (annex I of Reg. EU 2021/1165) is on the card; here the confirmation.
TourFert1 = Kind of product: fertiliser, soil improver, manure, corroborant...
TourFert2 = The Dolibarr product for the stock.
TourFert3 = Allowed in organic farming, with the category of annex II of Reg. EU 2021/1165.
TourFert4 = Nitrogen content: used for the nitrogen applied per hectare.
TourFert5 = For liquids: the density, to convert litres into kilograms.
TourCropplan1 = The cultivated plot.
TourCropplan2 = The crop, with its EPPO code.
TourCropplan3 = Start and end of the cycle: treatments are recorded only on plans in progress at the date.
TourCropplan4 = Estimated yield: used in the mass balance of the organic registers.
TourTreatment1 = Plant protection treatment or fertilisation.
TourTreatment2 = The farm; areas and products are added after saving.
TourTreatment3 = Date and time of start. More than 30 days after the treatment the record is late.
TourTreatment4 = Who applied the treatment: the register checks the licence.
TourTreatment5 = The machine used: the register checks the functional check of the sprayer.
TourTreatment6 = For organic farms: the document justifying the plant protection product (technical report, bulletin...).
TourHarvest1 = Le plan de production récolté.
TourHarvest2 = The harvested product that goes in stock.
TourHarvest3 = Quantity and unit.
TourHarvest4 = The lot. For organic or in conversion products it gets the suffix -BIO or -INCONV at the validation.
TourBio1Title = The registers
TourBio1 = Stock in and out, mass balance, summary by plot, seeds, inputs, treatments, purchases, harvests and sales.
TourBio2Title = Filters
TourBio2 = Farm, year or period, and for the stock register also warehouse, organic status and product.
TourBio3Title = Prints
TourBio3 = PDF and CSV of the register, and the annual organic dossier with all the sections for the control body.
